\pard\tx0\tx0\tx567\tx1134\tx1701\sl312\slmult1\pardirnatural\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \cb3 Quarto install almost everything required (you can use it to manage Pandoc, LaTeX, Graphviz, Mermaid and other tools all-in-one). For LaTeX it can install and update\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://yihui.org/tinytex/"}}{\fldrslt TinyTeX}}, allowing a small install footprint and automated addition of packages from CTAN. If you want to use R then you must install it yourself.\
